---
// Foundations
import Wrapper from "@/components/fundations/containers/Wrapper.astro";
import MailerLiteSignup from "@/components/forms/MailerLiteSignup.astro";
---

<section class="lozen-home-section lozen-home-section--tight bg-white">
  <Wrapper variant="standard" class="py-0">
    <div class="lozen-home-container lozen-home-container--wide">
      <div class="lozen-home-feature-panel lozen-home-feature-panel--navy">
        <div
          class="grid gap-0 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.98fr)_minmax(320px,0.52fr)]"
        >
          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-12 xl:p-14">
            <p class="lozen-home-eyebrow">AI Governance & Retention Risk</p>

            <h2 class="lozen-home-title mt-5 text-white sm:mt-6">
              AI is increasing workload.
            </h2>

            <div class="mt-5 max-w-3xl sm:mt-6">
              <p class="lozen-home-deck text-base-100">
                The Power User Trap℠ begins when high performers become the informal validation layer for AI adoption. They learn the tools first, troubleshoot failures, verify outputs, train colleagues, and absorb the cognitive burden while standard productivity metrics show improvement.
              </p>

              <p class="lozen-home-deck mt-4 text-base-100">
                The organization sees adoption. It does not see the epistemic load and concentration of oversight work. By the time the exit appears in retention data, the institutional knowledge has already left.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-7 max-w-xl sm:mt-8">
              <p class="lozen-home-card-meta text-accent-300">
                Download the Power User Trap℠ Brief
              </p>

              <div class="mt-3">
                <MailerLiteSignup
                  formId="power-user-brief-download"
                  group="poweruser"
                  theme="dark"
                  buttonLabel="Send the brief"
                  successMessage="Thank you. You can download the Power User Trap℠ brief here."
                  downloadHref="/download/Lozen_PowerUserTrap_Brief.pdf"
                  downloadLabel="Download the Power User Trap℠ brief"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <aside
            class="border-t border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6 sm:p-8 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:p-10"
          >
            <p class="lozen-home-card-meta text-accent-300">
              What your data misses
            </p>

            <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:mt-6">
              <div class="lozen-home-card lozen-home-card--navy lozen-home-card--quiet">
                <p class="lozen-home-card-title text-[1.05rem] text-white">
                  Oversight burden
                </p>
                <p class="lozen-home-card-body mt-3">
                  The work of checking, correcting, and validating AI output falls on the employees already trusted to exercise judgment. It is invisible to the organization because no system was designed to capture it.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="lozen-home-card lozen-home-card--navy lozen-home-card--quiet">
                <p class="lozen-home-card-title text-[1.05rem] text-white">
                  Invisible implementation work
                </p>
                <p class="lozen-home-card-body mt-3">
                  Training colleagues, troubleshooting tools, and maintaining workflow quality accumulate outside job descriptions, workload models, and compensation structures. The company sees productivity. It does not see the burden.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="lozen-home-card lozen-home-card--navy">
                <p class="lozen-home-card-title text-[1.05rem] text-white">
                  Retention exposure
                </p>
                <p class="lozen-home-card-body mt-3">
                  Productivity appears to rise while leadership capacity erodes. The risk becomes visible only after the person exits. Until then, the work is absorbed, uncompensated, and unrecorded.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Wrapper>
</section>
